&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Plume&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Plume, we believe that technology isn&#39;t about moving faster, it&#39;s about making life’s moments better. Which is why we’ve built the world&#39;s first, and only, open and hardware-independent service delivery platform for smart homes, small businesses, enterprises, and beyond. Our SaaS platform uses WiFi, advanced AI, and machine learning to create the future of connected spaces—and human experiences—at massive scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We now deliver services to over 60 million locations globally and have managed over 3 billion devices on our platform. We’re expanding rapidly, pioneering a new category, and we achieved our Series F funding in just four years. Our customers include many of the world&#39;s largest Internet Service Providers (ISPs) who look to Plume to help them evolve their smart home offerings while gleaning insights from their own data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;With a bias for action and a love for being trailblazers, the team at Plume embodies a combination of relentless curiosity and imaginative innovation. We challenge ourselves to think in ways that other companies don&#39;t, work to do what should be done (rather than what can), and if we can’t do it exceptionally well, we don’t do it. It’s how we&#39;ve assembled a team of world-class builders, thinkers, and doers. And it’s how we’re reinventing what’s possible every day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Role Description:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;Plume works with Internet Service Providers (ISPs) to run the connected experience inside their&lt;br&gt;subscribers’ homes and small businesses. Our platform sits between their network and the people using&lt;br&gt;it, managing WiFi performance, security, device visibility, care and the digital services layered on top. We&lt;br&gt;are used at scale by some of the largest ISPs across North America, Europe, Asia and the Middle East.&lt;br&gt;The UK and Ireland are mature and concentrated markets. The number of ISPs that matter is small, they&lt;br&gt;are well known to us, and most already have an established approach to managing the connected home.&lt;br&gt;Success here depends on building credibility at a senior level, shaping how these organisations think&lt;br&gt;about the experience they deliver to their subscribers, and then proving that value at scale.&lt;br&gt;We are looking for someone who is at their best in a small number of large, complex accounts rather&lt;br&gt;than in a broad prospecting territory.&lt;br&gt;It is a role with real ownership. You will be the face of Plume in the region, working directly with our&lt;br&gt;executive team and with senior leaders at some of the best-known ISPs in the market.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A named list of UK and Ireland ISPs, covering both new logos and the growth of existing&lt;br&gt;deployments into new services, subscriber tiers and lines of business.&lt;br&gt;• A multi-million-dollar annual quota carried across new business and installed base expansion.&lt;br&gt;• The full cycle: executive access, discovery, business case, technical validation and POC,&lt;br&gt;commercial modelling, procurement, contract, and a clean handover into delivery. You stay&lt;br&gt;accountable through launch.&lt;br&gt;• The relationship map inside each account. Not a single champion, but the CTO, the Chief Product&lt;br&gt;or Consumer officer, the owner of customer care and operations, and whoever holds the broadband&lt;br&gt;P&amp;amp;amp;L.&lt;br&gt;• A virtual team pulled from solutions engineering, product, delivery, finance, legal and executive&lt;br&gt;sponsorship. You direct it. You do not wait for it.&lt;br&gt;• Accurate forecasting. Deals of this size move, and we would rather know early than late.&lt;br&gt;• A clear read on the market: how ISPs in the region are approaching the connected home, where&lt;br&gt;their priorities are shifting, and what that means for our roadmap. You are our eyes in the territory.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role calls for someone who already understands how ISPs buy. Their decision cycles, stakeholder&lt;br&gt;structures and commercial models are specific to the industry, and the experience we are looking for&lt;br&gt;reflects that.&lt;br&gt;• A track record selling hardware, software, cloud or platform solutions directly to ISPs, with evidence&lt;br&gt;of recurring or subscription-based commercial models. Your experience should be with ISPs as the&lt;br&gt;buyer, rather than with a telco’s enterprise IT function as one account among many.&lt;br&gt;• Ownership of deals in the multi-million-dollar ACV range, with 9 to 24 month cycles, formal&lt;br&gt;procurement, and an established solution already in place.&lt;br&gt;• Fluency in ISP economics. ARPU and attach rates, churn and retention drivers, cost to serve,&lt;br&gt;contact volumes and handling time, truck roll avoidance, CPE fleet lifecycle and ODM relationships,&lt;br&gt;NPS. You should be able to build a credible business case yourself before a solutions engineer is in&lt;br&gt;the room.&lt;br&gt;• Experience winning business where the customer already had a solution in place, whether bought&lt;br&gt;or built in-house. That is a different commercial conversation, and we place real weight on it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• Existing senior relationships across UK and Ireland ISPs, or a specific and realistic plan for building&lt;br&gt;them inside two quarters.&lt;br&gt;• MEDDPICC applied in practice rather than in theory. Expect to walk us through a live deal from your&lt;br&gt;current role against it.&lt;br&gt;• Comfort operating without a finished playbook. Our product moves, our commercial models evolve,&lt;br&gt;and parts of this territory are still being defined. You will be building as you sell.&lt;br&gt;• Consistent quota attainment, and the ability to explain honestly where you missed and why.&lt;br&gt;• Willingness to travel regularly across UK and Ireland, and occasionally across EMEA.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Plume&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As the creator of the only open, hardware-independent, cloud-controlled experience platform for ISPs and their subscribers, Plume partners with over 400 ISP customers, including some of the world’s largest such as Charter, Liberty Global, and J:COM.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Using OpenSync, the most widely supported open-source, silicon-to-cloud framework for smart spaces, Plume’s software-defined network allows ISPs to decouple their service offerings from hardware and rapidly curate and deliver new services over a multi-vendor, open-platform architecture.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Plume is an equal opportunity workplace that maintains a continuing policy of nondiscrimination in all employment practices and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;decisions, ensuring equal employment opportunities for all qualified individuals without regard to &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;race, color, creed, religion, sex, national origin, age, physical or mental disability, sexual &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;orientation, gender identity, marital status, pregnancy, childbirth or related individual conditions, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;medical conditions (as defined by state law), military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local law. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
